<%# The one navigation the shell carries, grouped rather than a single list:
    Documentation is the guides listed as documents (Doc::GUIDES, which is not
    every markdown file that ships: the naming guide is read at /name and is
    listed there, in the top nav, instead of twice), and Reference is the
    gallery's own renderers. The same sidebar renders on both kinds of
    page, so a document links to the gallery and the gallery links back to
    every document, the way the exemplar's docs and reference sections sit
    side by side.

    A decision is not a guide: a guide is read to learn how to use Janela, a
    decision is the record of why it is shaped the way it is, and listing all
    of them here (there are dozens) swamped the one list that actually needs
    browsing at a glance. So Documentation names the guides individually and
    the decisions get a single link to their own index, where the full list
    already lives with its status and date beside each one. "Every decision"
    is the footer's own phrase for that same link (see shared/_footer), reused
    rather than invented again, so the site says one thing. %>
<nav class="shell-nav" aria-label="Reference">
  <div class="shell-nav-group">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <ul>
      <li><%= link_to "Overview", docs_path, class: (current_page?(docs_path) ? "current" : nil) %></li>
      <% Doc.guides.each do |doc| %>
        <li><%= link_to doc.nav_label, doc_path(doc.slug), class: (current_page?(doc_path(doc.slug)) ? "current" : nil) %></li>
      <% end %>
      <li><%= link_to "Every decision", docs_path(anchor: "decisions") %></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="shell-nav-group">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reference</p>
    <ul>
      <% Janela.renderers.each do |renderer| %>
        <li><%= link_to t("janela.renderers.#{renderer}"), gallery_path(anchor: "gallery-#{renderer}") %></li>
      <% end %>
      <li><%= link_to "Vitral", vitral_path, class: (current_page?(vitral_path) ? "current" : nil) %></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>
